    category: "longevity",
    summary: "Loop 001 daily digest for 2026-10-26, generated from research-watcher output/latest/hits.jsonl (114 hits, scan regenerated 2026-10-26 06:03 KST, Monday axis: aging-fibrosis-metabolism-single-cell/spatial-clinical translation). The score-9 top band was again fully recycled against the retained id:132-id:136 window (GSE281463/GSE281464/GSE281465 GWAS-chromatin bundle, GSE328275 TNBC immune atlas, GSE328422 sequential LN metastasis, GSE326553 Oprm1-A118G CosMx atlas all already featured), so today's harvest drops to the score-7 and score-6 ladder after the mandatory accession-dedupe against the page-level GSE retention set (comm -23 of hits.jsonl accessions against page.tsx accessions, 73 NOVEL accessions remain). Signal 1 is GSE328206, a Mus musculus lifespan-resolved Epi Multiome bundle (ATAC + gene expression, n=80 across lifespan strata, raw H5/MTX/TSV, pdat 2026/10/05): the watcher's highest-scoring NOVEL human-translation-adjacent aging dataset today, and the first such bundle in the retention window because the id:131-id:136 entries covered AR-degrader, P-selectin senolytic nanotherapy, IPF, and muscle-aging rather than a chromatin-level liver-aging regulatory atlas. Signal 2 pairs GSE348584 (n=15) with GSE348919 [Visium ST] (n=14), the imaging-resolution and transcriptome-resolution arms of a single preinvasive breast cancer study (pdat 2026/09/25 and 2026/09/29, both raw-available): a matched Xenium-style spatial atlas and Visium ST atlas of preinvasive disease, which is exactly the escalation-window geometry BB's refractory-cancer lane needs - the point where a clone acquires the spatial phenotype that predicts treatment failure - and no prior digest entry has carried a preinvasive-breast spatial pair. Signal 3 is GSE255312, a 72-sample human MASH liver spatial transcriptomics landscape (pdat 2026/10/06, raw-available CSV/DCC/PKC): the largest human fibrosis-lane cohort in today's NOVEL set and a direct feed into the fibrosis service lane, sitting alongside the id:136 IPF entry as a second, non-pulmonary fibrosis axis rather than a repeat. Lane coverage across the three picks is 1 x longevity, 1 x clinical/translational (preinvasive oncology), 1 x fibrosis (MASH), which preserves the 3-lane diversity standard set on the prior cycles. Brown Biotech read: the actionable value today is a matched-modality pair (Signal 2) and a lifespan-stratified epigenetic atlas (Signal 1), both of which can move straight into the multiomics intake pipeline without a new assay-design cycle; Signal 3 needs a QC notebook pass first given the mixed CSV/DCC/PKC supplementary layout.",
